{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KvwLoxzCt7jvVqinsQ8oct","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /tmp/arena-ws.SfiLYf/SOLUTION.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08d59dd4-b1ce-4bcf-8c96-50a81cec7993","uuid":"9e5b6a73-9351-409c-9399-6935d08b1d84","timestamp":"2026-07-25T15:24:44.823Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/tmp/arena-ws.SfiLYf/SOLUTION.md","content":"# Solution\n\nTwo bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`, both in the recency bookkeeping.\n\n## 1. `get` did not count as a \"use\"\n\n`get` returned the value without reordering the `OrderedDict`, so a key's\nposition only ever reflected when it was *written*, never when it was *read*.\nThat makes the cache least-recently-**inserted** rather than least-recently-used:\nreading `\"a\"` then inserting a new key still evicted `\"a\"`. Fixed by calling\n`self._data.move_to_end(key)` on a successful (non-expired) lookup, matching the\ndocstring's \"Both `get` and `put` count as 'use'\".\n\n## 2. `put` evicted on updates to existing keys\n\nThe capacity check `if len(self._data) >= self.capacity` ran unconditionally, so\noverwriting a key that was *already present* first popped the LRU entry. Since\nthe following assignment reused the existing slot rather than adding one, the\ncache silently shrank and an unrelated key was lost — `put(\"y\", 3)` on a full\ncache destroyed `\"x\"`. Fixed by only evicting when the key is genuinely new\n(`if key not in self._data and len(...) >= self.capacity`).\n\n`python3 -m pytest -q` now passes (6 passed).\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdP1PyPRKaUwN25DNun3z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `python3 -m pytest -q` reports **6 passed**.\n\nBoth bugs were in `lrucache/cache.py`'s recency bookkeeping:\n\n1. **`get` didn't refresh recency** (`cache.py:23`) — it returned the value without reordering the `OrderedDict`, so entries were ranked by insertion time, not use time. That made it a least-recently-*inserted* cache. Added `move_to_end(key)` on a successful, non-expired lookup.\n\n2. **`put` evicted on in-place updates** (`cache.py:32`) — the capacity check ran unconditionally, so overwriting an existing key popped the LRU entry first and then reused the existing slot, shrinking the cache and destroying an unrelated key. Now it only evicts when the key is actually new.\n\n`SOLUTION.md` written with the same explanation. I didn't touch `tests/` and made no commits."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":656,"cache_read_input_tokens":24815,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":656,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"08d59dd4-b1ce-4bcf-8c96-50a81cec7993","uuid":"a47bcabc-b989-4be9-a59f-b49595cd9ee3","timestamp":"2026-07-25T15:24:50.402Z","request_id":"req_011CdP1PuyHXubhCCDA9qcod"}
